fix: declare the sidePanel permission

`chrome.sidePanel.open()` throws when `sidePanel` is not in `permissions`, and
the call site caught the throw and logged it to a service-worker console nobody
is watching. The symptom was therefore identical to the previous commit's: a
click that appears to do nothing.

Both bugs had to be fixed for the panel to open, and neither was visible from
the other. The first was "no code asks to open the panel"; this one is "the
code asks and the browser refuses".

`tests/build-output.test.ts` gains a check that every privileged API the built
worker calls has a matching permission. The mapping is a hand-written table
rather than derived from the bundle, because API usage cannot be extracted from
minified output reliably; a table that fails loudly when a new API appears beats
a clever check that quietly covers less than it looks like. Verified by removing
the permission and confirming the test names it.
